  "gaps": {
    "_comment": "Known holes, tracked so the emitter's loud-fail is expected, not a surprise.",
    "spo2_RESOLVED_2026-08-11": "plan.pdhc now HAS an oxygen-saturation concept (spo2 = 2f15ae94-209e-4b0c-81bd-c91d76e74475, created during the asthma home-monitoring build), so spo2 is now bound above to the pdhc_vitals.v1 pulse_oximetry observation (DV_PROPORTION, |numerator). NOTE: the DV_PROPORTION FLAT emission (numerator only; denominator/type assumed template-fixed at 100/percent) has NOT been round-trip-validated on the sandbox yet — #507 proved DV_QUANTITY (temp/BP) only. Validate spo2 on openehr.phanera.se before enabling delivery.",
    "pending_template_extension": {
      "_comment": "#502 (2026-08-01): per-template PENDING archetype bindings. As of 2026-08-22 the anthropometry (5), lung_function (1) and laboratory (24) entries carry DRAFT binding_kind + target_flat_path (fixed_quantity) or analyte_cluster_path (repeating_analyte) per docs/openehr_flat_opt_field_map_502.md. These are NOT read by resolve() — promote into the live per-template registry after the .opt web template is captured (see that doc's coder checklist). Diagnoses/medications/care_events remain name+archetype only (later tickets, need clinical-modelling judgement). #728 M2 (2026-11-19): medications, care events and CGM promoted into the live registry; diagnoses moved to condition_sourced; only the unnamed concept remains.",
      "79a6cd4b-1af4-4c05-8f08-e5487a262237": {
        "concept_name": "Asthma finding",
        "target_template": "pdhc_diagnoses.v1",
        "target_archetype": "openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis.v1",
        "note": "#728 M2 2026-11-19: this plan.pdhc concept has NO display text and no explanation. The operator must name it before it can be modelled; it stays a gap and is NOT treated as a CDR-sourced diagnosis."
      }
    }
  },
